Challenge Overview

This challenge demonstrates weak access control using predictable user IDs and MD5 hashes.

---

Recon

Credentials were found in the page source and used to log in.

After login, the application redirected to:


?id=3000


The application used MD5 hashes of numeric IDs to identify users.

---

Analysis

Intercepted the requests using Burp Suite.

Discovered that the application relied on hashed IDs.

---

Exploitation

Generated MD5 hashes for IDs from 3000 to 3020.

Used Burp Suite Intruder to test the generated hashes.

Found the following hash belonging to the admin account:

4110a1994471c595f7583ef1b74ba4cb

Reversed the hash using CrackStation:


3013 -> 4110a1994471c595f7583ef1b74ba4cb


---

Result

The admin ID was:
3013

